## 3. Full migration checklist (including the fog/camera fixes)

| ✅ | Item | What to do |
|---|------|------------|
| 1 | **Package** | `npm uninstall mapbox-gl && npm install maplibre-gl` |
| 2 | **Imports / CDN** | `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';`  <br>or `<script type="module">import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';</script>` |
| 3 | **Namespace** | Replace **all** `mapboxgl` → `maplibregl` (including CSS class prefixes). |
| 4 | **Access token** | Delete `mapboxgl.accessToken = '…'`. |
| 5 | **Style URL** | Use a non-Mapbox style (e.g. `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty` or your own style JSON). |
| 6 | **Fog → Sky** | Replace every `map.setFog(...)` with `map.setSky(...)` (see code above). |
| 7 | **Free-camera → CameraOptions** | Replace `get/setFreeCameraOptions` with `calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation` + `jumpTo/easeTo/flyTo`. |
| 8 | **Other v2-only calls** | Search for `setProjection('globe')`, `setTerrain({exaggeration})`, etc., and use the MapLibre equivalents. |
| 9 | **Plugins** | Verify each Mapbox plugin works with MapLibre; if not, swap to a MapLibre-native fork (e.g. `maplibre-gl-geocoder`, `maplibre-gl-draw`). |
|10| **Geocoding / Directions** | Replace Mapbox APIs with Nominatim, Photon, OSRM, OpenRouteService, or a commercial provider (MapTiler, Pelias, etc.). |
|11| **CSS** | Update any custom CSS that targets `.mapboxgl-…` → `.maplibregl-…`. |
|12| **Testing** | Load the map, open the dev-tools console, and verify there are **no** `Uncaught TypeError: map.setFog is not a function` or similar errors. |
|13| **Style validation** | Run `npx gl-style-validate style.json` (install `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-style-spec` if needed) to catch any leftover Mapbox-only source URLs or layer names. |

---

## 4. Quick “fix-it” script for a typical codebase

If you have a large repo and want to automatically replace the most common v2 patterns, you can run a simple **search-and-replace** (e.g. with `sed`, `perl`, or an IDE). Below is a Node-script you can drop into `scripts/replace-mapbox-v2.js` and run with `node scripts/replace-mapbox-v2.js`.

```js
// scripts/replace-mapbox-v2.js
const fs = require('fs');
const path = require('path');
const glob = require('glob');

const files = glob.sync('src/**/*.js'); // adjust pattern to your code layout

files.forEach(file => {
  let src = fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');
  let changed = false;

  // 1️⃣ mapboxgl → maplibregl
  if (src.includes('mapboxgl')) {
    src = src.replace(/\bmapboxgl\b/g, 'maplibregl');
    changed = true;
  }

  // 2️⃣ setFog → setSky (basic property rename)
  src = src.replace(/\.setFog\(\s*{([^}]*)}\s*\)/g, (match, body) => {
    // naive conversion – you may need to tweak values manually
    const props = body
      .split(',')
      .map(p => p.trim())
      .map(p => {
        const [k, v] = p.split(':').map(s => s.trim());
        const map = {
          color: '"fog-color"',
          'high-color': '"horizon-color"',
          'space-color': '"sky-color"',
          'horizon-blend': '"horizon-fog-blend"',
          // add more mappings if you used them
        };
        return `${map[k] || `"${k}"`}: ${v}`;
      })
      .join(', ');
    return `.setSky({${props}})`;
  });

  // 3️⃣ FreeCameraOptions → calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation
  src = src.replace(
    /const\s+cam\s*=\s*new\s+maplibregl\.FreeCameraOptions\(\);\s*([\s\S]*?)map\.setFreeCameraOptions\(\s*cam\s*\);/g,
    (match, inner) => {
      // This is a very rough heuristic – you’ll probably need to edit manually.
      // It assumes you later assign cam.position and cam.orientation.
      const posMatch = inner.match(/cam\.position\s*=\s*\[([^\]]+)\];/);
      const oriMatch = inner.match(/cam\.orientation\s*=\s*{([^}]+)}/);
      if (!posMatch || !oriMatch) return match; // give up

      const [lng, lat, alt] = posMatch[1].split(',').map(s => s.trim());
      const ori = oriMatch[1]
        .split(',')
        .reduce((obj, kv) => {
          const [k, v] = kv.split(':').map(s => s.trim());
          obj[k] = v;
          return obj;
        }, {});
      const bearing = ori.bearing || 0;
      const pitch = ori.pitch || 0;
      const roll = ori.roll || 0;

      return `
const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
  [${lng}, ${lat}], ${alt}, ${bearing}, ${pitch}, ${roll}
);
map.jumpTo(camOpts);
`;
    }
  );

  if (changed) {
    fs.writeFileSync(file, src, 'utf8');
    console.log(`✔ Updated ${file}`);
  }
});
```

> **Caution:** The script does a *best-effort* conversion. After running it

You haven’t “broken” anything – you’re just running into the **fundamental difference** between the two libraries.

### 1️⃣ Why the calls are missing

| What you used in Mapbox GL JS v2 | What exists in MapLibre GL JS |
|----------------------------------|------------------------------|
| `map.setFog({...})` (and the `fog` root-level style property) | **No `fog` API**. MapLibre introduced a different atmospheric model called **`sky`**. The equivalent call is `map.setSky({...})` and the style property is `sky`. |
| `map.getFreeCameraOptions()` / `map.setFreeCameraOptions()` (or the `FreeCameraOptions` class) | **No free-camera API**. MapLibre’s camera is described by `CameraOptions` (`center`, `zoom`, `pitch`, `bearing`, `elevation`, `roll`). To position the camera from a 3-D lng/lat/alt/rotation you use the helper `map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(...)` (or the older `calculateCameraOptionsFromTo`) and then pass the result to `jumpTo`, `easeTo` or `flyTo`. |

So the migration isn’t “wrong”; it’s just that those v2-only methods never existed in the MapLibre code base (MapLibre forked from Mapbox GL JS v1.13).

---

## 2️⃣ How to replace the missing features

#### a. Atmospheric fog → `sky`

```js
// Mapbox GL JS v2
map.setFog({
  "color": "white",
  "high-color": "#add8e6",
  "space-color": "#d8f2ff",
  "horizon-blend": 0.3
});
```

```js
// MapLibre GL JS (v6+)
map.setSky({
  // sky-color = space-color
  "sky-color": "#d8f2ff",
  // horizon-color = high-color
  "horizon-color": "#add8e6",
  // fog-color = color
  "fog-color": "white",
  // blend factors – adjust to taste
  "fog-ground-blend": 0.5,
  "horizon-fog-blend": 0.5,
  "sky-horizon-blend": 0.5,
  "atmosphere-blend": 1.0
});
```

*The `sky` spec is documented here:* https://maplibre.org/maplibre-style-spec/sky/  
*API reference:* https://maplibre.org/maplibre-gl-js/docs/API/classes/Map/#setsky  

If you only need a simple fog-like look, you can set just `sky-color`, `horizon-color`, and `fog-color` and leave the blend values at their defaults.

#### b. Free-camera positioning → `calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation`

```js
// Mapbox GL JS v2 (example)
const cam = map.getFreeCameraOptions();
cam.position = [lng, lat, altitude];
cam.orientation = [pitch, bearing, roll];
map.setFreeCameraOptions(cam);
```

```js
// MapLibre GL JS (v5+)
const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
  [lng, lat],          // lng/lat of the camera
  altitude,            // altitude in meters above the ground
  bearing,             // bearing (0-360)
  pitch,               // pitch (0-85)
  roll ?? 0            // roll (optional, default 0)
);

// Now move the view – choose the animation you prefer
map.jumpTo(camOpts);   // instant
// or
map.easeTo(camOpts);   // smooth
// or
map.flyTo(camOpts);    // globe-aware flight
```

If you need a “look-at” from point A to point B you can also use the older helper:

```js
const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromTo(
  [fromLng, fromLat], fromAltitude,
  [toLng,   toLat],   toAltitude
);
map.easeTo(camOpts);
```

*API docs:* https://maplibre.org/maplibre-gl-js/docs/API/classes/Map/#calculatecameraoptionsfromcameralnglataltrotation  

---

## 3️⃣ Quick sanity-check checklist for a full migration

| ✅ Step | What to verify |
|--------|----------------|
| **Package** | `npm uninstall mapbox-gl && npm install maplibre-gl` (or use the CDN module version). |
| **Imports / CSS** | `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';` and `import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';` (v6 is ES-modules only). |
| **Namespace** | All `mapboxgl` → `maplibregl` (including class names in CSS: `mapboxgl-ctrl` → `maplibregl-ctrl`). |
| **Access token** | Remove any `mapboxgl.accessToken = '…'`. |
| **Style URL** | Replace `mapbox://styles/...` with a non-Mapbox style (e.g. `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty` or your own style JSON). |
| **Fog → Sky** | Replace every `map.setFog(...)` with `map.setSky(...)` (adjust property names). |
| **Free camera → CameraOptions** | Replace `get/setFreeCameraOptions` with the `calculateCameraOptions…` helper + `jumpTo/easeTo/flyTo`. |
| **Plugins** | Verify each Mapbox plugin works; if not, swap to a MapLibre-native fork (see the **awesome-maplibre** list). |
| **Mapbox APIs** | Switch geocoding, routing, etc. to open alternatives (Nominatim, OSRM, OpenRouteService, MapTiler, etc.). |
| **CSS class overrides** | If you wrote custom CSS targeting `.mapboxgl-…`, rename to `.maplibregl-…`. |
| **Test** | Load the map, check that controls appear, that the style renders, and that any fog/sky or camera moves behave as expected. |

If you run through the checklist and still see errors, the most common culprits are:

* **Forgot to change the style URL** – a `mapbox://` style will 404 because MapLibre can’t fetch Mapbox-hosted tiles without a token.
* **Left a stray `mapboxgl.accessToken` line** – it does nothing in MapLibre but can be confusing when debugging.
* **Using a Mapbox-only plugin** – many UI plugins (e.g., `mapbox-gl-geocoder`) need a MapLibre-compatible fork (`@maplibre/mapbox-gl-geocoder` or `maplibre-gl-geocoder`).

---

## 4️⃣ Example: Minimal working map after migration

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre migration demo</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any public style that serves vector tiles
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12,
    pitch: 45,
    bearing: -17
  });

  // Sky (fog) replacement
  map.on('load', () => {
    map.setSky({
      'sky-color': '#d8f2ff',
      'horizon-color': '#add8e6',
      'fog-color': 'white',
      'fog-ground-blend': 0.5,
      'horizon-fog-blend': 0.5,
      'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5,
      'atmosphere-blend': 1.0
    });
  });

  // Example of free-camera positioning
  const goTo3D = () => {
    const cam = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
      [-122.42, 37.78], // lng/lat
      500,              // altitude (m)
      -17,              // bearing
      45,               // pitch
      0                 // roll
    );
    map.flyTo(cam);
  };

  // Fly to the 3-D view after the style loads
  map.once('styledata', goTo3D);
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

*Run this in a modern browser (MapLibre v6 requires WebGL 2). The map loads, shows a sky/fog effect, and flies to a 3-D camera position.*

